title: Righteousness Exalteth a Nation – Nations and the Believer
description: God's judgment on nations, and the believer in them: nations judged by their works and individuals by faith, God's law for nations, judgment for innocent blood, sodomy an abomination, nations judged by the works of Christians among them, subject to the higher powers, and liberty that comes only from Christ, from the teachings on nations.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-nations.html
highlight: nation; land

# One deck for the doctrine "Nations & the believer" (97 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- Righteousness Exalteth a Nation [title]
overline: Doctrine · Righteousness exalteth a nation
heading: Nations and the Believer
sub: God's judgment on nations, and the believer in them.
refs: Proverbs 14:34; 2 Chronicles 7:14; Matthew 5:13; Romans 13:1; Galatians 5:1
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 12265, 10127
--- Nations by works, individuals by faith
big: Proverbs 14:34 | mark: Righteousness exalteth a nation
p: God judges nations based on their works. Even as He judges individuals based on their faith. It's an important distinction to keep in mind as we rightly divide the word of God.
p: All of God's covenants with the Hebrew are if/then ([[Exodus 15:26]]). This is the covenant with nations, with the people on this earth. God judges us as individuals spiritually by faith, but God judges nations on earth by their works.

# from 14786
--- Judged here on this earth
big: Zephaniah 2:3 | mark: Seek ye the LORD, all ye meek of the earth
p: The judgment of man comes after our physical death (*and it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment*, [[Hebrews 9:27]]). But the judgment of nations is here on this earth, and is a collective judgment of the people in their land.
p: The prophets are sent by God with warnings and rebuke, calling the lost to repentance, nations to reform, kings to fear the Lord.

=== God's law for nations
# from 6700
--- Babel: scattered into nations
kicker: God's law for nations
big: Genesis 11:8 | mark: the LORD scattered them abroad from thence upon the face of all the earth
p: The people imagined a vain thing. A tower to Heaven. That they could work their way to Heaven and be like God.
p: We are meant to be in nations. Nations by clan. By blood. Not one world government, full of vanity. Not even by a civic nationalism of paper and statutes that erases who we are, *making a name for ourselves*.

# from 13087
--- God's commands for the king
kicker: God's law for nations
big: Deuteronomy 17:15 | mark: one from among thy brethren shalt thou set king over thee
p: The king shall be one He chooses, not a stranger or foreign influence. A brother. In modern practice, this would preclude putting a non-believer in charge.
p: He shall not multiply horses to himself, a cavalry that is a false sense of security, emboldening the people to turn from trusting in God's mighty hand to defend them.

# from 11425, 11426
--- The law of God is perfect
kicker: God's law for nations
big: Leviticus 20:22 | mark: that the land, whither I bring you to dwell therein, spue you not out
p: The purpose was to separate the people unto God and away from the error, whoredoms and abominations of the other nations. To be holy because He is holy.
p: The law of God is perfect. His judgments are righteous. A just nation seeking after the Lord, who have the fear of God, would implement these strictures and punishments, that their nation not be judged. These laws give us insight to the perfect will of God for a people.

# from 11096, 17520
--- Restitution, and judgment speedily
kicker: God's law for nations
big: Ecclesiastes 8:11 | mark: Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily
p: Robbery was punished by restitution plus a fifth part, and a trespass offering. That's it ([[Leviticus 6:4-5]]).
p: The refusal to judge rightly and swiftly is why crime and perversion are rampant today. It all starts with shielding the wicked from the consequence of their actions. This keeps them from fearing God.
read: app:doctrine-nations~6700 | Babel: God scattered them into nations
read: app:doctrine-nations~11425 | God's civil law still judges nations
read: app:doctrine-nations~11096 | Restitution, not prisons: God's just law

=== Judgment for innocent blood
# from 12748, 13101, 13115
--- Blood defileth the land
kicker: Judgment for innocent blood
big: Numbers 35:33 | mark: for blood it defileth the land
p: The foundation of God's law is justice, and the avoidance of shedding innocent blood. His mercy is extended to His people, who if they receive it must make provision for the innocent, and punish those who subvert the system.
p: If a murderer seeks sanctuary falsely, he is turned over to die the death, because that is how the blood of the innocent is atoned. *Whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed* ([[Genesis 9:6]]).

# from 11373, 12014
--- Through the fire to Molech
kicker: Judgment for innocent blood
big: Leviticus 18:21 | mark: thou shalt not let any of thy seed pass through the fire to Molech
p: Sacrifice of children to false gods was a common practice in every age and nation. Today it is done through abortion. In Canaan, they sacrificed to Moloch. Today, it is often Mammon. It is horribly wicked.
p: Again and again we see God's judgment poured out on nations that shed innocent blood, child sacrifice as part of worshiping false gods being the worst example of this ([[Jeremiah 32:35]]).

# from 17275
--- The fields of the fatherless
kicker: Judgment for innocent blood
big: Proverbs 23:10-11 | mark: enter not into the fields of the fatherless: For their redeemer is mighty
p: Taking land from the fatherless, stealing the inheritance of those who have no one to stand for their cause. This evil will be rewarded by God; He shall plead their cause.
p: Jezebel killed Naboth by false witnesses for his vineyard. God sends Elijah: dogs will lick Ahab's blood where they licked Naboth's ([[1 Kings 21:19]]).
read: app:doctrine-nations~13101 | Put away the guilt of innocent blood
read: app:doctrine-nations~11373 | Abortion: passing children through the fire

=== Sodomy an abomination
# from 11375
--- The land vomiteth out her inhabitants
kicker: Sodomy an abomination
big: Leviticus 18:24-25 | mark: the land itself vomiteth out her inhabitants
p: God tells us specifically the acts, sexual perversions, fornication, adultery, incest, bestiality, sodomy, that cause the land itself to visit the iniquity on the people, and spew them out.
p: Child sacrifice, worshiping false gods, sodomy, sexual depravity. These are the causes of nations being destroyed.

# from 14506, 13158
--- Sodomites in the land
kicker: Sodomy an abomination
big: 1 Kings 14:24 | mark: there were also sodomites in the land
p: Whenever people fall away from the true God and take up false gods and idols, even under the guise of worshiping Him, it provokes the Lord. But allowing sodomites to exist and commit their filthy abominations is even more wicked, and God punishes nations for it.
p: Some teach falsely that this is only about temple prostitution, a contrivance to justify sodomites. The verse is clear. Whores and sodomites are not allowed among the children of Israel ([[Deuteronomy 23:17]]).

# from 13806, 13807, 10559
--- Benjamin protected them
kicker: Sodomy an abomination
big: Judges 21:25 | mark: every man did that which was right in his own eyes
p: Judges 19–21 deals directly with the evil of allowing sodomites free reign in a nation. The Levite's concubine, defiled and slain by these dogs, became a national outrage.
p: The tribe of Benjamin protected the sodomites, and God gave the others of Israel victory over them for condoning and protecting these wicked sons of Belial. It is very illustrative of the times we live in.

# from 10535
--- Josiah broke down their houses
kicker: Sodomy an abomination
big: 2 Kings 23:7 | mark: he brake down the houses of the sodomites
p: Good kings came occasionally, and did what was right in the sight of the Lord, and when they did, they bought their people reprieve, as God repented for a time of the evil He was to do.
read: app:doctrine-nations~11375 | The land vomiteth out her inhabitants
read: app:doctrine-nations~10559 | Benjamin protected the sodomites

=== Nations judged by their works
# from 11806
--- The potter's power over nations
kicker: Nations judged by their works
big: Jeremiah 18:7-8 | mark: If that nation, against whom I have pronounced, turn from their evil, I will repent of the evil
p: While many take the potter analogy and make it about us as individuals, because God does shape us for His purpose, the primary application here, and in [[Romans 9]], is about nations, specifically the physical nation of Israel.

# from 11546, 16150
--- God hates idols among His people
kicker: Nations judged by their works
big: Leviticus 26:1 | mark: Ye shall make you no idols nor graven image
p: Those who call themselves by His name who bow before statues of stone, molten and graven idols, are what spark His wrath. Open idolatry is worse than secret ([[Ezekiel 8:12]]).
p: Catholicism and Orthodox Christianity, so called, the apostates who reject salvation by grace and set up images to be served and bowed before, are the leading reason why Europe and America are suffering today.

# from 15661, 15639
--- Children are their princes
kicker: Nations judged by their works
big: Isaiah 3:4 | mark: I will give children to be their princes
p: A lack of righteous judges and men of honor, of prophets and wise elders. In their place are children. And the children rise up against their elders, and promote the base, the morally wicked.
p: When a people have turned from the true faith, even the most performative forms of worship become a burden to them. *When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell corn?* ([[Amos 8:5]]). We see that today in America.

# from 14556, 11914
--- Ahab humbled himself
kicker: Nations judged by their works
big: 1 Kings 21:29 | mark: because he humbleth himself before me, I will not bring the evil in his days
p: Ahab, upon hearing the judgment of the Lord, humbled himself before God. And God does soften His judgment, forestalling His wrath during Ahab's time.
p: But the wine cup of God's fury came on Judah and all the nations of the region, Babylon serving as God's tool to pour out His wrath ([[Jeremiah 25:15]]).
read: app:doctrine-nations~12265 | Nations judged by works, individuals by faith
read: app:doctrine-nations~11546 | God hates idols among His people

=== Judged by Christians' works
# from 11605, 12900
--- If my people
kicker: Nations judged by Christians' works
big: 2 Chronicles 7:14 | mark: If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves; heal their land
p: The judgment of nations is by their works, and more, the fruit of those among them that call themselves by His name.
p: This promise is extended to every nation that has Christians living in it. And every nation on earth has saved Christians among them. Or those apostates calling themselves by His name, yet chasing idols and drunk on the fornications of their mother church.

# from 17851, 16308
--- Ye are the salt of the earth
kicker: Nations judged by Christians' works
big: Matthew 5:13 | mark: Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour
p: We are given eternal life by faith in Christ Jesus alone. But our lives on this earth are judged by the good that we do.
p: What other nation has been made as fair as America? Shot up like the cedars, *his heart is lifted up in his height* ([[Ezekiel 31:10]]). When judgment comes is entirely up to saved believers. We are the salt of the earth, but so many have lost their savour.

# from 16173, 15649
--- Noah, Daniel, and Job
kicker: Nations judged by Christians' works
big: Ezekiel 14:14 | mark: Though these three men, Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it
p: As Abraham argued with the Lord concerning Sodom, the presence of the righteous is generally sufficient to stave off judgment, at least for a time. We preserve the world. But a land as backslidden as Judah: only the righteous themselves are saved.
p: *Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD* ([[Isaiah 1:18]]). We are the righteous remnant.

# from 15233, 15240
--- Hezekiah's revival
kicker: Nations judged by Christians' works
big: 2 Chronicles 30:9 | mark: the LORD your God is gracious and merciful, and will not turn away his face from you, if ye return unto him
p: A standing promise to Christians, from a God who cannot lie, who runs to meet the prodigals coming home to Him.
p: The turning towards the Lord by all the people, and their zeal, results in smashing the idols in the land ([[2 Chronicles 31:1]]).

# from 4692, 1833
--- Revival starts with the children of light
kicker: Nations judged by Christians' works
big: Ephesians 5:8 | mark: walk as children of light
p: Why as a nation are we failing, slouching to Gomorrah? Is it the children of darkness? Or is it the people who call themselves by His name, not shining the light but walking after the ways of the unbelieving? Compromising, and so being compromised.
p: If you want that judgment to reverse or slow down even a little, it doesn't depend on what the degenerate unsaved people do. It depends on what the saved Bible believing Christians do. And the primary thing is winning souls to Christ.

# from 3412, 6731
--- Turning toward the Lord is all we have
kicker: Nations judged by Christians' works
big: Acts 26:18 | mark: To open their eyes, and to turn them from darkness to light
p: All other methods of delaying the wrath that America deserves are vanity. We cannot vote our way out. We cannot shoot our way out. We cannot riot and exact our own vengeance.
read: app:doctrine-nations~17851 | Ye are the salt of the earth
read: app:doctrine-nations~1833 | Nations blessed or bred out by God

=== Subject to the higher powers
# from 10971, 1103, 14972
--- The powers that be are ordained of God
kicker: Subject to the higher powers
big: Romans 13:1 | mark: Let every soul be subject unto the higher powers
p: God puts the people in power over us, to His purpose. Even the wicked. God uses good rulers and bad rulers to enact judgment on the people for their sin, collectively.
p: Of course we are to follow the higher law of God when earthly authority contradicts it; we ought to obey God rather than men ([[Acts 5:29]]). Think of Daniel. He never compromised what was right, yet even under evil powers, he prospered.

# from 6338, 10974
--- Render to Caesar
kicker: Subject to the higher powers
big: Mark 12:17 | mark: Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar’s, and to God the things that are God’s
p: Not paying taxes and breaking the law regarding how they are administered, even to a church, is a sin. You can pray they be lowered. You can be thankful God has made your church exempt.
p: But a so-called pastor in a living room church, refusing to obey the law and encouraging others to do the same, almost always is a false prophet ([[Romans 13:7]]).

# from 9017, 1143, 4160
--- Not weak: Paul in chains
kicker: Subject to the higher powers
big: Acts 16:28 | mark: Do thyself no harm: for we are all here
p: Paul was stoned, snuck out of cities in baskets lest the mobs led by Jews tear him apart, and wrote most of his epistles from chains. He could have escaped the Philippian jail, but stayed to get the jailer saved. To glory in persecution for His name's sake isn't “compromised and weak”; it's the only way we win.
p: We live of no offense. Paying tribute. Paying custom. Not breaking the law, until the law is explicitly anti-Christ. Make them say your salvation is hate.

# from 10973, 4164, 17217
--- Live worthy of a godly nation
kicker: Subject to the higher powers
big: Proverbs 16:12 | mark: the throne is established by righteousness
p: When I hear the fearful and angry calling for insurrection, I see their lack of faith. And of this sin, I am chief.
p: Live worthy of a godly nation, and remember that God's wrath is in His time. The biggest delay is having a people worth saving because they turned to the Lord. That's on you. That's on me.
read: app:doctrine-nations~10971 | Let every soul be subject unto the higher powers
read: app:doctrine-nations~9017 | Paul's subjection and boldness
read: app:doctrine-nations~10974 | Render tribute: not paying taxes is sin

=== Liberty comes from Christ
# from 11019
--- No liberty outside of Christ
kicker: Liberty comes from Christ
big: Galatians 5:1 | mark: Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free
p: The blessings of liberty come from the liberty found in Christ. There is no liberty outside of Christ. It isn't a concept to be understood and maintained in a secular setting. It has no meaning without the Gospel, the beautiful law of liberty.

# from 13026, 13027
--- Not every man right in his own eyes
kicker: Liberty comes from Christ
big: Deuteronomy 12:8 | mark: every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes
p: The blessings of liberty come from those who believe on the Lord, know His word and follow it. Not from every man doing what is right in their own eyes.
p: There are Internet theologians who claim the law of Israel was libertarian. That is a lie. God has laws. God puts government in place. The more godly the people, the greater the blessings of liberty. The freer we are. The more moral and just.

# from 17371, 13983, 10972
--- No political solution to a spiritual problem
kicker: Liberty comes from Christ
big: Proverbs 28:2 | mark: For the transgression of a land many are the princes thereof
p: The iniquity and sin in a country results in *many princes*: more and more oppression and rules and rulers. A sinful people get the leadership they deserve.
p: The means of government is incidental to the hearts of the people. Monarchy, democracy, socialism, a dictatorship: none of it matters if we are not a godly people ([[1 Samuel 12:24-25]]). We cannot vote our way out.

# from 13043
--- Everything is downstream from God
kicker: Liberty comes from Christ
big: Deuteronomy 13:4 | mark: Ye shall walk after the LORD your God, and fear him
p: Everything is downstream from a people's relationship with God. He judges individuals by His grace and their faith, and nations by their works.
p: Free speech in a society Christian enough that unbelievers feel uncomfortable challenging basic decency, works. Where Christians are a looked down upon remnant, it doesn't. The blessings that allow these freedoms come from liberty in Christ.

# from 13037
--- No freedom of religion in the Kingdom
kicker: Liberty comes from Christ
big: Exodus 20:3 | mark: Thou shalt have no other gods before me
p: There is no “freedom of religion” in the Kingdom of Heaven ([[Deuteronomy 13:6-9]]). No one can force conversion by the sword, only by the word. Freedom from state religion is good, and right.
p: But idolatrous sects, pagans, Jews, satanic cults, perverse groups who reject the God of our fathers, should never have been given the freedom to spread their abominations. This will be enforced in the Millennium. Amen.
read: app:doctrine-nations~13037 | No freedom of religion in the Kingdom
read: app:doctrine-nations~13043 | Everything is downstream from God

=== If my people
--- Heal Their Land [title]
overline: Nations & the believer
heading: Heal Their Land
big: 2 Chronicles 7:14 | mark: then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land
center: Turning to the right or left leads to destruction. Turning towards the Lord is all we have.
read: topic-judgment | The Judgment Seat – Judgment, Hell and the Resurrection
note: Every teaching is on the [[app:doctrine-nations|Nations & the believer]] page.
